   "bars": 4,
   "development": "Bell and quiet hats. The choir alone hums the hook's shape: basses, then tenors, then altos (Fm, Db, C)."
  },
  {
   "id": "command",
   "bars": 4,
   "development": "The drop. THRONE//VOLT states the V3 hook, low and sparse; the organ answers in its rests."
  },
  {
   "id": "tension",
   "bars": 3,
   "development": "Groove B. The hook climbs to Ab4 over a Neapolitan Gb; a few singers join the organ's answers."
  },
  {
   "id": "breath",
   "bars": 1,
   "development": "V2's hole. The choir alone and close: Bbm9, C7sus4, C7b9, then a breath of silence."
  },
  {
   "id": "divine",
   "bars": 4,
   "development": "The slam. Low lead calls, high wide choir answers, full-organ hits; the plagal amen resolves to F major."
  }
